CM_ "Leapmotor B10 (2025, global market), reverse engineered from comma rlogs. Checksums are AUTOSAR E2E Profile 2 with per-message constants (see CHECKSUM comments). Each signal comment says CONFIRMED (matched filmed actions or a dedicated test), INFERRED or WEAK.";
CM_ SG_ 388 WHEEL_SPEED_FL "CONFIRMED: positions from filmed figure-eights: front/rear rises from 1.02 straight to 1.27 near lock, and the left wheels run faster when steering right. Scale matches GPS within 0.1 km/h at a filmed steady 30 km/h. within about 1% of GPS above 60 km/h up to 126 km/h. Width at least 14 bits; no wrap in about 11 hours of logs.";
CM_ SG_ 388 WHEEL_SPEED_FR "CONFIRMED: positions from filmed figure-eights: front/rear rises from 1.02 straight to 1.27 near lock, and the left wheels run faster when steering right. Scale matches GPS within 0.1 km/h at a filmed steady 30 km/h. within about 1% of GPS above 60 km/h up to 126 km/h. Width at least 14 bits; no wrap in about 11 hours of logs.";
CM_ SG_ 388 WHEEL_SPEED_RL "CONFIRMED: positions from filmed figure-eights: front/rear rises from 1.02 straight to 1.27 near lock, and the left wheels run faster when steering right. Scale matches GPS within 0.1 km/h at a filmed steady 30 km/h. within about 1% of GPS above 60 km/h up to 126 km/h. Width at least 14 bits; no wrap in about 11 hours of logs.";
CM_ SG_ 388 WHEEL_SPEED_RR "CONFIRMED: positions from filmed figure-eights: front/rear rises from 1.02 straight to 1.27 near lock, and the left wheels run faster when steering right. Scale matches GPS within 0.1 km/h at a filmed steady 30 km/h. within about 1% of GPS above 60 km/h up to 126 km/h. Width at least 14 bits; no wrap in about 11 hours of logs.";
CM_ SG_ 563 YAW_RATE "INFERRED scale, sign CONFIRMED: positive = turning left (openpilot convention); raw rises when turning right, r +0.994 to +1.000 against the comma gyro (livePose.angularVelocityDevice.z, positive right) on 3 traces. R2 0.993-0.999 against livePose on 5 datasets. Fit gives 0.0196; 0.02 assumed.";
CM_ SG_ 389 LONG_ACCEL "INFERRED: R2 0.70-0.95 against livePose on 5 datasets. Same encoding as the Leapmotor T03 DBC (10 bits, offset -16), which matches the earlier 9-bit signed reading over the logged range. No wrap down to -6.8 m/s^2.";
CM_ SG_ 589 DISPLAY_SPEED "CONFIRMED: equal to the filmed dashboard speed in 6 of 6 checks (50, 70, 100 km/h). Reads about 3.5 percent above the wheel speeds, as dashboards do.";
CM_ SG_ 675 DRIVER_SEATBELT_UNLATCHED "CONFIRMED: 1 when the driver belt is unbuckled. Followed 4 of 4 buckle actions in a live capture (cluster warning 0x24D bit 146 0.5 s later), the filmed belt step of recording 1, and read 0 (buckled) at every seatbeltNotLatched refusal caused by the old signal. Constant over whole drives with the belt on.";
CM_ BO_ 552 "Rear-left blind-spot radar (20 Hz, silent when stopped). Bytes 8-15 carry object data when something is detected.";
CM_ SG_ 552 OBJECT_DETECTED "CONFIRMED on video: on 3 of 3 checked episodes a car appeared in the left lane beside the B10 in the road camera within 1 s of the flag clearing. Set in 8.5% of driving above 50 km/h, less often while signalling left (drivers wait for a clear lane).";
CM_ BO_ 554 "Rear-right blind-spot radar, same layout as BSD_LEFT (0x228).";
CM_ SG_ 554 OBJECT_DETECTED "INFERRED by symmetry with BSD_LEFT: same layout, set in 0.7% of driving above 50 km/h (in right-hand traffic you are rarely overtaken on the right). The one checked episode was not conclusive on video.";
CM_ SG_ 397 DRIVER_OVERRIDE "INFERRED: the EPS flags strong driver input. Set during both filmed driver overrides of LCC (0.4-0.5 s before LCC released) even though STEER_TORQUE_DRIVER only reached 2-3; otherwise set 66% of the time when |STEER_TORQUE_DRIVER| >= 15 and under 0.4% below 8. Short bursts. Also set whenever the car is above about 121 km/h, with or without the driver (on at 121.5, off at 120.1 km/h; 99% of frames above 121 km/h on a stock drive), so it only means driver input below that. The EPS still follows the steering request up there: openpilot steered at up to 134 km/h with it set.";
CM_ SG_ 397 ADAS_LKA_RECEIVED "CONFIRMED by the camera-unplug test: 1 while the EPS receives ADAS_LKA (0x83) from the camera, 0 with the camera unplugged (and for the first 0.2 s after ignition, before the camera starts). Bit 60 sets at the same time. Used as a temporary steering fault: the EPS is not receiving a valid steering frame.";
CM_ SG_ 397 ADAS_LKA_TIMEOUT "CONFIRMED by the camera-unplug test: 3 with the camera unplugged (no ADAS_LKA), 0 when it is received; also 3 for the first second after ignition.";
CM_ SG_ 397 STEER_ANGLE "CONFIRMED by filmed holds: raw moves about 4450 per 90 deg and 9000 per 180 deg. Sign CONFIRMED: positive = left (openpilot convention); raw rises to the right (r +0.98 against the comma gyro in the figure-eights). Factor is negative so openpilot reads left-positive. Lock is about -515/+522 deg, or 2.9 turns, which the driver confirmed. Centre 32490 from the filmed centre holds; a few counts may remain.";
CM_ SG_ 397 STEER_SPEED_ABS "INFERRED: one count is about 202 raw per second, or 4.04 deg/s, R2 0.99 or better on 5 datasets; 4 assumed, the same as the Leapmotor T03 DBC. Magnitude only, no sign.";
CM_ SG_ 397 STEER_TORQUE_DRIVER "INFERRED: driver steering torque, positive = left (openpilot convention). Raw 57 and 100 while held still at left and right lock, exactly 78 hands off; raw rises when steering right (r +0.54 to +0.81 with the steering rate on 3 traces). Hands-off LCC never exceeds 3, manual steering while moving reaches 7 (p90) to 20. Unit unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 131 "Layout INFERRED from 396,908 frames on 16 traces (5 days): 166 of 256 bits never change; every bit that is not always zero is defined here, so unpack-then-pack reproduces recorded frames exactly. 50 Hz, sent by the ADAS unit.";
CM_ SG_ 131 ACC_STATE "INFERRED, strong: 3 while ACC/LCC engaged, 2 when ACC is ready, 1 when not ready (Park, brake pressed) or overridden by the accelerator while engaged (96-100% of those frames have the pedal pressed, on 8 traces).";
CM_ SG_ 131 ACC_ACCEL_REQ "INFERRED, strong: the ACC acceleration request. Leads the measured acceleration (0x185 LONG_ACCEL) by about 250 ms, r +0.85 to +0.96 on 8 traces; fit gives zero at raw 99.9 and 0.045 m/s^2 per step (0.05 used, residual 0.08 m/s^2). Raw 100 (0) whenever not engaged.";
CM_ SG_ 131 ACC_OVERRIDE "INFERRED: set exactly when ACC_STATE drops to 1 while engaged, i.e. accelerator override (frame-for-frame match on 8 traces).";
CM_ SG_ 131 ASSIST_OFF_2 "INFERRED: identical to ASSIST_OFF on every frame.";
CM_ SG_ 131 CONSTANT_72 "CONSTANT: 125 (0x7D) on every recorded frame. Meaning unknown; must be sent as-is.";
CM_ SG_ 131 CONSTANT_152 "CONSTANT: 125 (0x7D) on every recorded frame. Meaning unknown; must be sent as-is.";
CM_ SG_ 131 UNKNOWN_90 "UNKNOWN: 28 on nearly every frame; a handful of other values. Copied from the camera frame.";
CM_ SG_ 131 STEER_ANGLE_REQ "INFERRED, strong: the LCC steering angle request, same encoding as STEER_ANGLE (positive = left; r 1.000 with it). On 5 routes it leads the measured angle (0x18D) by 70-100 ms while LCC steers, and the request-minus-measured gap tracks the LCC torque (r +0.35 to +0.59). In manual driving it lags by 20-30 ms, so it echoes the measured angle when not steering. Sent by the ADAS unit (its own clock, with 0x142/0x229/0x2D1/0x2D5). No torque request found in this frame. The camera sends it (it vanished with the camera unplugged), and the EPS followed openpilot's copy both ways with LCC_STEERING_ACTIVE_COPY set and the LCC_RAMP word.";
CM_ SG_ 389 SEATBELT_REMINDER "INFERRED, NOT the belt state: matches the belt only before READY. While driving it follows standstill (0 when stopped, 1 when moving) with the belt buckled, which made openpilot refuse to engage from a stop. Use SEATBELT.DRIVER_SEATBELT_UNLATCHED.";
CM_ SG_ 656 BLINKER_LEFT "CONFIRMED by filmed step order: left, right, then hazards. Flips every 0.40 s. Both blinker bits on means hazards.";
CM_ SG_ 656 BLINKER_RIGHT "CONFIRMED by filmed step order: left, right, then hazards. Flips every 0.40 s.";
CM_ SG_ 656 DRIVER_DOOR_OPEN "CONFIRMED once by filmed door opening; 1 for 11.5 s. Bit 46 did the same, so one may be another door or a lamp.";
CM_ BO_ 183 "Bits 16 and 28 set when the camera is unplugged (probably ADAS unavailable). Every bit that is not always zero is defined (UNKNOWN_* fields copied as-is), so unpack-then-pack reproduces recorded frames exactly; needed to send the camera a cancel copy of this frame.";
CM_ SG_ 183 STALK_PUSH "CONFIRMED by stated order, parked: 1 is a single push (ACC), 2 is a double push (LCC, passing through 1 first), each held about 1 s. INFERRED: 3 is pushing the stalk up, which the driver says cancels assist. All 14 logged value-3 pushes during assist ended it within about 0.25 s.";
CM_ SG_ 183 TORQUE_DEMAND "WEAK: rises with acceleration (r 0.78-0.84), but stayed at 0 during 3 filmed accelerator presses in Park. Probably torque demand. Drops to 0 whenever the accelerator is released, even while slowing at -1.5 m/s^2, so it carries no regen.";
CM_ SG_ 182 ACCEL_PEDAL "CONFIRMED by 3 filmed presses in Park, peak 254 each. Scale 0.4 percent per count as in the Leapmotor T03 DBC, so 254 is about 100 percent. One-pedal mode was off for this test.";
CM_ SG_ 182 BRAKE_PRESSED "CONFIRMED by 3 filmed presses in Park. Ends assist, as the driver says: both logged cases within 0.01 s. One-pedal mode was off for this test. Rarely on while slowing on earlier routes, which the driver says were almost always in one-pedal mode.";
CM_ SG_ 182 GEAR "CONFIRMED by filmed shifts and the dashboard. Earlier routes agree: 1 moves only backward, 0 and 2 never move, 3 only forward.";
CM_ SG_ 390 BRAKE_PRESSURE "INFERRED: bytes 2-5 are identical, peaks 51-57 on 3 filmed presses, near 0 otherwise. In filmed braking tests it stayed near 0 for much of the time the pedal was pressed, which suggests blended braking (regen first, friction later). Unit unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 183 ASSIST_ENGAGED "INFERRED: 1 in all 15 assist periods on 5 routes, including 1 ACC-only period, 0 elsewhere while driving. Also matched a route not used in the search: on 0.6 s after the push, off 0.6 s after the cancel.";
CM_ SG_ 589 ASSIST_ENGAGED_COPY "INFERRED: same behaviour as 0xB7 bit 30.";
CM_ SG_ 131 ASSIST_OFF "INFERRED: exact inverse of ASSIST_ENGAGED on 5 routes. Bit 44 behaves the same.";
CM_ SG_ 589 LCC_ENGAGED "INFERRED: on 95-100% of LCC periods, off in the ACC-only period and when not engaged. Only 1 ACC-only period tested.";
CM_ SG_ 397 LCC_STEERING_ACTIVE "INFERRED: never on outside LCC, on for 54-100% of it, so possibly when LCC is steering. Not checked against the dashboard.";
CM_ SG_ 131 LCC_STEERING_ACTIVE_COPY "INFERRED: same behaviour as 0x18D bit 67.";
CM_ SG_ 397 STEER_TORQUE_EPS "INFERRED: exactly 1000 raw when LCC is not steering on most routes, 939-1074 when it is, follows byte 10 (r 0.82-0.91). Possibly the torque applied by LCC. Unit unknown. Sign INFERRED: positive pushes the wheel right, negative left (stock LCC, 90,000 samples on 3 routes: the angle moves the opposite way to the value, r -0.20 to -0.37; confirmed by the stage-2 steering steps). Also moved during a probable lane-departure correction with assist off.";
CM_ SG_ 322 FCW "INFERRED, strong: forward collision warning from the front camera. On for 1.5-3.3 s at the driver's reported warnings (2 of 2, route 00000261), each time about 2 s before the driver braked hard; ACC was off. About 13 rising edges per drive on 29 earlier drives. 0x229 bit 110 switches with it.";
CM_ SG_ 322 SPEED_LIMIT "CONFIRMED against filmed road-sign icons (90, 110): matches once a 1-2 s video timing difference is allowed. Values 20-130 in tens. A brief 50 lasting 0.6 s was not seen on the dashboard. 0 and 255 appear rarely and may mean none or invalid.";
CM_ SG_ 131 LCC_RAMP "CONFIRMED on the car (needed to steer left, and sets the EPS torque authority), meaning INFERRED: bytes 16-17 as one word. 0x7801 on every frame without LCC steering. While LCC steers it moves along a ladder of 254 per step (one step per frame): about 31 steps when it starts (0.5-0.6 s), deeper with lateral acceleration and speed, always 25-46 steps; steps = 19.1 + 9.94 * |lateral accel m/s^2| + 0.112 * speed km/h fits 142,234 stock frames (R^2 0.83). It jumps back to 0x7801 when LCC stops. The EPS torque range grows with the step count (about +/-10 early in the ramp, +/-45 at 30, +/-70 at 42-46). Earlier read as three fields; the top 4 bits are what looked like an LCC state (7 off, 6 engaging, 5 active, 4 curve). With the idle word plus the steering bit, the EPS followed openpilot's angle to the right only; with a fixed 30 steps it steered both ways but could not hold a curve at 75 km/h (torque flat at 61).";
CM_ SG_ 131 ACC_SET_SPEED "CONFIRMED: equal to the filmed green ACC badge in 6 of 6 checks (50, 70, 100 km/h), steps with knob rotation. Scale 0.2 km/h, unlike the 0.1 of the Leapmotor T03.";
CM_ SG_ 388 CHECKSUM "CONFIRMED: AUTOSAR E2E Profile 2, as opendbc volkswagen_mqb_meb_checksum: crc=0xFF; for bytes 1..end: crc=CRC8H2F[crc^b]; crc^=K[counter]; crc=CRC8H2F[crc]; checksum=crc^0xFF. K is a 16-entry table per message in checksum_constants.json, learned on route 0000022d and exact on every tested frame of 3 other routes from 2 other days.";
CM_ SG_ 388 COUNTER "CONFIRMED: rolling 0-15, one step per frame.";
CM_ SG_ 563 CHECKSUM "CONFIRMED: AUTOSAR E2E Profile 2, as opendbc volkswagen_mqb_meb_checksum: crc=0xFF; for bytes 1..end: crc=CRC8H2F[crc^b]; crc^=K[counter]; crc=CRC8H2F[crc]; checksum=crc^0xFF. K is a 16-entry table per message in checksum_constants.json, learned on route 0000022d and exact on every tested frame of 3 other routes from 2 other days.";
CM_ SG_ 563 COUNTER "CONFIRMED: rolling 0-15, one step per frame.";
CM_ SG_ 397 CHECKSUM "CONFIRMED: AUTOSAR E2E Profile 2, as opendbc volkswagen_mqb_meb_checksum: crc=0xFF; for bytes 1..end: crc=CRC8H2F[crc^b]; crc^=K[counter]; crc=CRC8H2F[crc]; checksum=crc^0xFF. K is a 16-entry table per message in checksum_constants.json, learned on route 0000022d and exact on every tested frame of 3 other routes from 2 other days.";
CM_ SG_ 397 COUNTER "CONFIRMED: rolling 0-15, one step per frame.";
